{
  /*
   * The UI half of the package: React cards, and nothing else.
   *
   * WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE TSCONFIG
   * -------------------------------
   * `tsconfig.json` deliberately omits "dom" from `lib` so that touching
   * `window`, `document` or `localStorage` inside decode/gospel/settings is a
   * COMPILE ERROR rather than a runtime surprise in whichever app imported
   * the package second. That guard is the point of the package and must not
   * be weakened.
   *
   * React cards genuinely need the DOM lib -- a `<div onClick>` does not
   * typecheck without it. Widening the base config would hand DOM globals to
   * decode/gospel/settings as well and quietly delete the guard. So the DOM
   * lib is granted HERE, to `src/ui` only, and the logic modules keep
   * compiling against ES2020 alone.
   *
   * The rule for anything under src/ui: it may use the DOM for RENDERING, but
   * it must not read or write `localStorage`, call transport, or otherwise
   * reach for app state. Cards take what they draw as props. Each app keeps
   * its own back end and passes it in -- that is why these files can be
   * shared at all.
   */
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "lib": ["ES2020", "DOM"],
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "rootDir": "src",
    "outDir": "dist"
  },
  "include": ["src/ui"],
  "exclude": ["src/ui/**/__tests__/**", "dist", "node_modules"]
}
